# keymaps — keyboard shortcut reference

## Ghostty splits  (Hyper = Caps Lock held = Ctrl+Alt+Cmd)

    Hyper + |          new split right
    Hyper + -          new split down
    Hyper + hjkl       navigate between splits
    Hyper + Shift+hjkl resize split
    Hyper + w          close split
    Hyper + z          zoom / unzoom split
    Hyper + =          equalize splits
    Hyper + `          toggle quick terminal (global)

## AeroSpace windows  (Option = ⌥)

    Option + hjkl          focus window left/down/up/right
    Option + Shift+hjkl    move window left/down/up/right
    Option + 1..9          switch to workspace N
    Option + Shift+1..9    move window to workspace N
    Option + Tab           previous workspace (toggle)
    Option + /             toggle layout: tiles ↔ accordion
    Option + ,             toggle orientation: horizontal ↔ vertical
    Option + f             AeroSpace fullscreen (zoom within workspace — NOT macOS fullscreen)
    Option + Shift+Space   float ↔ tile current window
    Option + Esc           pause/resume AeroSpace daemon
    Option + Shift+;       enter service mode

### Service mode  (after Option+Shift+;)

    Esc                    reload config + exit service mode
    r                      flatten layout tree (reset all splits) ← the "undo everything" key
    Shift+hjkl             join window with neighbour (merge containers)

## Recovery — when confused

    Option + Shift+;  →  r       flatten layout tree, back to clean even split
    Option + f                   exit AeroSpace fullscreen (NOT macOS fullscreen)
    Cmd + Ctrl + F               exit macOS native fullscreen (green button mode)
    Cmd + Space → reopen app     if a window disappeared (was minimised — avoid minimise)

## Linux WM — future  (Super = ⊞ / same physical position as Option)

    Super + hjkl           focus window  (Hyprland / Pop Shell)
    Super + Shift+hjkl     move window
    Super + 1..9           switch workspace
    Super + Shift+1..9     move window to workspace

## Notes

- Hyper and Option namespaces never overlap — no toggle needed for coexistence.
- Option+Left/Right is intentionally NOT bound to AeroSpace (preserves word navigation).
- Cmd+H (hide) is safe — AeroSpace auto-unhides on next focus.
- Cmd+M (minimise) removes the window from the layout tree — avoid it.
- See docs/keybindings.md in the dotfiles repo for rationale and collision analysis.
